WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.440
- Welcome back, everybody!
(audience clapping)

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:04.080
It is National Sock Day, which was created

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.090
by the next three guests that are here.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:08.160
They're the founders of Pair of Thieves,

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.430
a clothing company that happens
to make super comfy socks.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.450
If you know me at all,

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.250
all my friends know that
I'm obsessed with socks.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.900
Like, you know people
get that for Christmas?

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.610
I love getting socks for Christmas.

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.250
Anyway, but you know,
family members are like,

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.210
why did you give me socks?

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.043
Give me socks.

00:00:22.043 --> 00:00:23.610
Anyway, and what started out
(audience laughing)

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:25.230
as a fun idea has turned into

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.840
a deeply meaningful mission,
which is even better.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.700
Please welcome Alan Stewart,

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.833
David Ehrenberg and
Cash Warren, everybody.

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:34.590
(audience cheering)

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.479
So, welcome to the show.

00:00:36.479 --> 00:00:37.376
- Thank you so much.

00:00:37.376 --> 00:00:38.850
- You guys have been friends for a minute,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.810
right?
- We have.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:40.710
We grew up together.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:44.011
You know, when I had the idea
to start Pair of Thieves,

00:00:44.011 --> 00:00:45.630
I knew I'm not a mister know-it-all,

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.040
I don't have all the answers.
- Yeah, I love it.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.870
- And so, I knew I needed partners

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.760
to take the idea and
make it a bit stronger.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.310
And so, I reached out
to two childhood friends

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:54.600
to help me launch.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:57.120
- We've been at this for
31 years of friendship.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.860
- Oh, my gosh.
- Yes.

00:00:58.860 --> 00:00:59.820
- I love those friends.
- And starting a business

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.840
is like a marriage.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:01.673
- Yeah.

00:01:01.673 --> 00:01:02.610
Well, sometimes it doesn't work out.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:03.711
I hope the best for you.

00:01:03.711 --> 00:01:05.940
(audience and guests laughing)

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:07.260
So I've heard.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.000
So, how did the sock thing happen?

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.900
Where did that come from?

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.070
Why socks?

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.250
- So, we knew there was an
opportunity to make better socks.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.410
When we started this, like, 10 years ago,

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:17.850
there just weren't good socks out there.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.710
And so, we said, can we take style,

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:22.260
performance and affordability
and mash them all up?

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.555
And that was what gave
birth to Pair of Thieves.

00:01:24.555 --> 00:01:26.310
- Yeah, I love the name too.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:27.330
It's such a cool name.

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:29.880
So, tell us about the cause behind this.

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:33.270
- Yeah, I mean, when we were
out one day as a company,

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.780
giving socks out to people in
need, living on the streets,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.180
we got this guy who
came up to me and said,

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:41.610
you know, these are like
gold when you're homeless.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.190
And so, at that moment, we
knew that something small

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.050
could turn into something big.

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:47.640
And since then, we've partnered up

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.280
with a great organization
called Baby2Baby,

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.920
and we've donated over
3 million pairs of socks

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:53.952
together.
- Wow.

00:01:53.952 --> 00:01:54.785
- Yeah.
(audience clapping)

00:01:54.785 --> 00:01:55.650
- You don't think about that,

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.130
but that would be something
that's, like, shoes or socks,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.960
like, I never really thought
about that, but that-

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.160
- It's super important.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.150
- Yeah.
- Super important,

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.830
and they have to be donated new.

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:08.520
You don't donate used socks,
and so it takes companies

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.880
like ours to step up and really
try to make a difference.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:12.713
- Yeah.

00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:15.420
- And so, we started National
Sock Day as kind of a fun,

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.940
lighthearted way to raise
attention and raise awareness.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.277
- How do you get a
national day for something?

00:02:20.277 --> 00:02:21.110
- It's really funny.
- It's so cool.

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:21.943
So, we were really jealous
(audience cheering)

00:02:21.943 --> 00:02:23.881
of tacos getting Tuesday.

00:02:23.881 --> 00:02:25.950
- (sighs) Love Taco Tuesday.
(audience laughing)

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.960
- So, we were like, how do
we get to one for socks?

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.810
And there is a National
Day Calendar organization

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:33.630
that governs all these
kind of random day holidays

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:35.460
that you see popping up everywhere.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.588
And we applied, we wrote an essay

00:02:37.588 --> 00:02:39.090
and of the 18,000-
- You wrote an essay.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.687
I've never seen you work harder.

00:02:40.687 --> 00:02:41.790
- I know, yeah, yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.332
- I will get this sock day!

00:02:43.332 --> 00:02:44.370
- (laughs) I will get it!
- I love it.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:45.480
- And we were awarded the day.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:48.090
And so, December 4 is National Sock Day.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.410
- Love it!
- Today, it is very much

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:51.450
a day of service for the company.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.430
We volunteer at organizations.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.470
This year, we're
volunteering at Baby2Baby.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.370
- Yeah.
- In the past,

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.320
we've donated at shelter partnerships

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.180
and a number of others.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.300
But it feels good to get
out and to really recognize,

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.620
something so small can make

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.120
the biggest difference in someone's life.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.670
- 100%, and how cool is it
that you get to do it with,

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.050
like, friends that you've grown up with

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:11.280
and you get to do something, like,

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.500
that you love to do together,
but also is an impact,

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.333
like, in the world?

00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:15.630
That's cool.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:17.490
Well, what's the bigger
mission of the company?

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:18.570
What's the big thing?

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:21.180
- So, you know, we started
out as a sock brand,

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:24.060
but as our products have
expanded to underwear

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:27.540
and to shirts and, you know,
the customer base has expanded,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:30.210
our give back has as
well, and so today we have

00:03:30.210 --> 00:03:33.090
a wonderful partnership
with an organization

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:36.270
called The Trevor
Project, for LGBTQ youth.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.403
- Yeah, yeah.
(audience clapping)

00:03:37.403 --> 00:03:41.340
- And, thank you, we donate
hundreds of thousands of dollars

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:44.280
in product to that
organization every year.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.130
We're all dads, and so teen mental health

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.960
is incredibly important to us.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.460
And so, we support an organization

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:54.000
called Bring Change to Mind,
and then as Alan mentioned,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.610
Baby2Baby is our partnership
for families in need.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:57.870
- Yeah, it's so funny.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.910
We all have children here.

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:01.590
I think when we were all kids,

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:03.150
mental health was still
a very important thing,

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:05.910
but I think social media has just

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.190
really just blown up everything.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.650
And it's more important now than ever

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.800
for kids to really have great self-esteem.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.450
All right, so how can
everybody get involved?

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:16.283
What should they do?

00:04:16.283 --> 00:04:17.550
- You know, in honor
of us being here today,

00:04:17.550 --> 00:04:19.620
we wanted to announce that, you know,

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:21.420
for December 4 and December 5,

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.400
everything on pairofthieves.com,

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.790
we'll donate 100% of our
net proceeds to charity.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.366
And so-
- Wow!

00:04:28.366 --> 00:04:29.199
- Thank you.
(audience clapping)

00:04:29.199 --> 00:04:31.440
So, if you're looking for a great gift,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:33.930
know that you're purchasing with a purpose

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:36.060
and we're gonna support organizations.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.100
- Purchasing with a purpose.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.420
That should be a shirt.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:40.770
It should be a sweatshirt y'all make.

00:04:40.770 --> 00:04:41.790
I would buy that too.
(Cash laughing)

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.380
That's so nice!

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.250
But that's really cool.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.930
Everybody, for more information

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.810
on how you can make a difference
this National Sock Day,

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:50.610
'cause they worked hard for that,

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:53.073
there was an essay, people,
head to our socials.

